# Coolify local secrets

Agents MAY read `.cursor/.env.deploy` or `.env.local` when Coolify or SSH access is needed (deploy, API token, server host) — **under Cursor**. Under Claude Code they may not: `.claude/settings.json` puts `Read(./.env)`, `Read(./.env.*)` and `Read(./.cursor/.env.deploy)` in `permissions.deny`, and `.env.local` matches `./.env.*`, so both files named above are refused by the harness. The deny list is the safer posture and stays; this paragraph exists so an agent does not spend a turn discovering it.

**When the read is denied.** Do not route around it — no `cat` through a shell, no guessing from `.env.example`, no substituting a value from another environment. Name the value you need and ask the operator for it, or point them at `/admin/integrations`: Coolify, GitHub and Cloudflare credentials belong in the encrypted `Integration` store, so for anything the application itself uses the admin UI is the right home rather than a local env file.

- Those files are gitignored. MUST NOT commit them.
- MUST NOT write passwords, SSH passwords, or full API tokens into source, docs, rules, or chat.
- MUST NOT echo secrets. After a token exists, report last4 only (`••••abcd`) and say "token stored".
- Public host `162.35.99.80` and `https://coolify.navroop.app` are not secrets.
- App code stores Coolify/GitHub/Cloudflare secrets encrypted on Prisma `Integration` (`lib/crypto.ts`). Configure them in `/admin/integrations`, not env.

```text
# ❌ BAD — paste Coolify/SSH password into a rule or AGENTS.md
# ✅ GOOD — read .cursor/.env.deploy in the agent session; keep values out of git
```
